          "id": "79201594f24295e86cd2a3ba411ca3d1401ec2fd",
          "message": "test(actor-scheduler): GreenSender::send timeout coverage (2026-07-29 audit) (#964)\n\n## Summary\n\nScheduled test-quality-control pass\n(`docs/bugs/2026-07-29-test-quality-audit-followup.md`), continuing the\nseries in `docs/bugs/`. Covers the 28 commits since the last pass\n(`d7d33b8..HEAD`).\n\n- **Static audit**: swept all 19 test files changed in this range\nagainst `docs/STYLE.md`'s \"Test Public API\" rule and the\ncomments/historical-narration rule. No violations found — the changes\nare rustfmt reflow, import reorders, or new tests built entirely from\npublic API.\n- **Mutation testing** (`cargo-mutants`) on the three genuinely new\npieces of logic in this diff range — nothing a prior pass had touched:\n- `pixelflow-core/src/lattice/cell_grid.rs` (new file): 6 missed mutants\n→ 0. Real gaps: a degenerate `rows=1` test fixture hid a\nmultiply-vs-divide bug in `cells_len`, coincidentally-equal fg/bg\nfixture values hid a per-channel buffer-index bug, the y-axis apron\nclamp had no test (only x was covered), and no test straddled the\nsum-vs-product grid-extent boundary.\n- `actor-scheduler/src/host.rs`: 1 missed → 0. `GreenSender::send` (new\nbackoff-based delivery path) had zero direct test coverage in this\ncrate.\n- `pixelflow-runtime/src/coordinator_node.rs` (new file): 2 missed → 0.\n`CoordinatorData`'s `Debug` impl was never exercised, and\n`present_cooked_frame`'s frame-number increment was checked for presence\nbut never for its actual value.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cargo test -p pixelflow-core --lib`: 112/112\n- [x] `cargo test -p actor-scheduler --lib`: 138/138\n- [x] `cargo test -p pixelflow-runtime --lib`: 64/64\n- [x] `cargo check --workspace`: clean\n- [x] `cargo fmt --check` on all touched crates: clean\n- [x] Re-ran `cargo-mutants` on all three files after the fixes to\nconfirm each gap is actually closed (numbers in the doc), not just that\nthe new tests pass\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_019AmfMxL8Rh2VF9uwZ7JF5e\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_019AmfMxL8Rh2VF9uwZ7JF5e)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
