          "distinct": true,
          "id": "453d2a6e53e7f31043c4a2db8a144d3a7914e45e",
          "message": "docs(plans): loop-aware codegen — give the register allocator the lattice (#1080)\n\n## Summary\n\nDesign-only plan (no code changes) for making the compiler loop/lattice\naware: `docs/plans/2026-09-01-loop-aware-codegen.md`.\n\n- Verifies the premise: `EmitCtx` is `{ max_regs: Option<u8> }`\n  (`pixelflow-codegen/src/emit/mod.rs:281-303`), and every non-default\n`with_max_regs` call site is a test (3 total) — every production path\nuses\n  `EmitCtx::default()`.\n- Works out what a compile-time lattice denotes relative to\n`pixelflow_core::lattice::Lattice`/`DiscreteManifold`'s\nrepresentable-functor\nlaw: same law, deliberately lossier projection\n(`loop_mask`/`exact_lanes`),\n  not the same concrete type — keyed against `jit_cache`'s window-resize\ncache-hit scenario so specialization doesn't blow up the compile cache.\n- What moves to compile time vs. stays dynamic at the ABI boundary\n  (`TileSlice`/`Point4`).\n- How the register allocator's `Vec<Def>` becomes a three-region\n  (prologue/row/batch) schedule with liveness across back edges, and how\nX-as-induction/Y-as-loop-state/Z,W-as-invariant become allocation facts\n  instead of hardcoded ABI positions (`coord_reg`, `SCAFFOLD_ACC`/\n  `SCAFFOLD_SCRATCH`).\n- Concrete deletions (`COORD_SLOTS`, the per-iteration coordinate\n  `slot_store`/`slot_load` pairs, unconditional hoist-to-memory).\n- A 4-stage migration, each with a checkable invariant (byte-identity\nwhere\nthe stage is a pure refactor, a structured diff + differential execution\n  where it isn't, and a JIT-bench regression gate for the stage that's\n  expected to actually change codegen).\n- Risks, including explicit sequencing against\n`docs/plans/2026-09-01-register-allocation-escape-hatches.md` (its step\n4\nis what this plan expands) and the escape-hatches plan's own\nregister-pool\n  findings.\n- An appendix addressing a related crate-layout question raised\nmid-design\n(should `Field` move out of `pixelflow-core`, given the real dependency\nchain is `ir → search → codegen → compiler → core`): corrects two of my\nown working claims against the actual code, finds the SIMD backend layer\n  is *already* fully `pub` and already has live external callers\n(`pixelflow-graphics`, 187 test call sites) independent of any crate\nmove,\n  and identifies that `Field` currently conflates a lane-free language\nprimitive with a register-sized ABI unit — with a recommendation to spec\nthat split as its own plan after this one's stages land, not to fold it\nin\n  here.\n\n## Test plan\n\nDocs-only change.\n\n- [x] `cargo fmt --all -- --check` — clean (no Rust files touched)\n- [x] `git diff --stat` against `main` shows only the new file under\n      `docs/plans/`\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
