          "distinct": true,
          "id": "38ea6eaadc0e18e764f55a9e14abd56b9796a44b",
          "message": "test(pixelflow-search): fix graph.rs CostModel test names; correct stale backlog note (#1049)\n\n## Summary\n\nScheduled test-quality-control pass, originally aimed at\n`pixelflow-search/src/egraph/cost.rs` (backlog item 1 from\n`docs/bugs/2026-08-26-test-quality-audit-followup.md`).\n\n**That item turned out to already be closed.** This branch was\naccidentally built from a stale local `origin/main` (a combined `git\nfetch` for two refs failed outright because one didn't exist, which\nsilently left the cached `origin/main` 15 commits behind). One of the\nmissed commits, `#1027` (2026-08-22 audit), had already closed the exact\nsame `cost.rs` mutation-testing backlog item with materially better\ntests\nthan the ones this pass wrote blind — including specifically avoiding an\n`unsafe std::env::set_var` flaw under a parallel test harness that this\npass's own first attempt reproduced.\n\nOnce caught (via `mergeable_state: dirty` on the first push), the branch\nwas reset onto the real current `main` and the redundant `cost.rs`\nchanges\nwere discarded entirely rather than merging a duplicate over #1027's\nbetter version.\n\n**What's left, and real:**\n- Two STYLE.md-noncompliant test names in\n`pixelflow-search/src/egraph/graph.rs`\n(`depth_penalty_calculation` →\n`depth_cost_should_apply_linear_penalty_only_above_threshold`,\n`shallow_cost_model` →\n`shallow_should_set_aggressive_depth_threshold_and_penalty`),\nexercising the same `CostModel` API from its own test file, which #1027\ndidn't touch. Dropped the now-redundant WHAT-comments alongside the\nrenames.\n- A corrected audit doc\n(`docs/bugs/2026-08-28-test-quality-audit-followup.md`)\nstriking the stale backlog item and recording why, so the next scheduled\n  pass doesn't repeat this.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `cargo test -p pixelflow-search --lib`: 183 passed, 0 failed, 2\nignored (against current `main`)\n- [x] `cargo clippy -p pixelflow-search --lib --tests -- -D warnings`:\nclean\n- [x] `cargo fmt -p pixelflow-search -- --check`: clean\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
