          "distinct": true,
          "id": "bffc2405fef47d4c0ddc4e40655b0384e82870b7",
          "message": "feat(pixelflow-ir): LatticeShape — the extents are the compile-time lattice (#1094)\n\n## Summary\n\nThree commits: the plan's second revision, stage 0′ implementing it, and\na fix for a launch regression stage 0′ introduced.\n\n`LoopShape` (landed in #1092) carried a 2-bit loop mask so a kernel\nstayed shared across a window resize. That property is rejected —\n**resizing is recompilation** — so the shape becomes the lattice's\n**extents**, and a differently-sized lattice is a different kernel. The\nplan revision also corrects a second error: coordinate axes and\nreduction indices are one binder nest, not two, exactly as `variance.rs`\nalready said.\n\n## Plan revision (`a893385f`)\n\n- **Extents are compile-time.** Measured price recorded: a full\n`jit_cache::compile` miss is 1.45 ms (8 nodes) to 39 ms (512 nodes) on\nthe host, and essentially all of it is saturation (emit is 13 µs to 1.5\nms). Recorded mitigation that keeps the decision: saturation does not\ndepend on extents, so saturate once per structure and extract once per\nextent.\n- **One binder nest.** A binder binds an index over a static extent and\neither **folds** (`Reduce`) or **stores** (a lattice axis). Scope,\nschedule, cost, liveness and interchange are shared; the schedule has N\nregions from the start.\n- **The denotation is the unrolled program**; a loop is its\nrun-length-encoded form. Every analysis is defined on the distributed\nform and computed on the factored one.\n- **Vocabulary: distribute (unroll) / factor (loop).**\n- **Peel is the unroll and the proof.** `⊕_{i<N+1} body = (⊕_{i<N} body)\n⊕ body[i := N]` applied N times is the unroll, and it is how the e-graph\nderived `Σ_{i<4} i² = 14` in #1092. `Σ_{i<N} i = N(N−1)/2` and `Σ_i c =\nN·c` are the factored statements of the same computation — lemmas, not\nseparate machinery. Both forms sit in one e-class, so **extraction\nchooses** unroll-versus-loop by comparing `N·cost(body) + (N−1)·cost(⊕)`\nagainst loop overhead. Substitution needs an explicit `Subst` node with\nthree rules, whose second rule (`Subst(e, i, k) = e` when `i ∉ deps(e)`)\nis `unroll_reduce`'s existing sharing of index-invariant subtrees. That\nis stage 1's IR question answered.\n\n## Stage 0′ (`70a0883e`)\n\n- **`LatticeShape([u32; 4])`** replaces `LoopShape`:\n`pixelflow_core::Lattice` with `origin` erased and nothing else erased.\n`varying()` gives the binders as a `Variance`; `key_bytes()` is the\ncache key.\n- `jit_cache::compile` and `optimize_runtime_arena` key on the extents.\n`JitManifold::call_collapse` debug-asserts the tile lies **within** the\nlattice (rows within Y, batches within `ceil(X / lanes)`).\n- `Lattice::bake` passes `self.extent`; per-batch `eval` paths pass\n`POINT`.\n- **`CellGridGeometry` gains `frame_w`/`frame_h`.** The cell-grid\nkernels are compiled for the frame's pixel lattice, so the frame size is\npart of the geometry; both bake paths check their `PlaneRegion` lies\nwithin it. core-term tracks the window size and recompiles when it\nchanges, which its geometry check already did for every other field.\n- The resize-sharing test is replaced by its opposite: same extents\nshare an entry, one more column does not.\n\n## Launch fix (`7146468e`)\n\nThe macOS launch-stability check went red on all 15 launches of\n`70a0883e`: core-term aborted seconds after the first frame. Two\ndefects, both from stage 0′:\n\n- `Surface::width_px` is **logical points** (the device-pixel size is\nthe separate `frame_width`/`frame_height`, which is what `window_keeper`\nsizes the `Frame` from). core-term recorded points as its frame lattice\nwhile the renderer bakes device pixels, so on any Retina scale the new\nregion-within-frame assert fired in a rasterizer worker thread and\n`panic = abort` killed the process. Before the first window event the\nlattice was `0×0` and it fired at any scale. The geometry now scales by\n`density`, the same conversion its other fields already make, and falls\nback to the grid's own extent when no window has been measured.\n- That assert is downgraded to `debug_assert`, matching\n`JitManifold::call_collapse`'s check of the same promise. Today's\nemitted code reads its loop bounds from the tile at run time, so a wider\nregion is a stale cache key, not wrong pixels. It becomes load-bearing\nwhen the code specializes on extents and should be promoted with that\nchange, not ahead of it.\n\n## Validation\n\nOn `70a0883e`: fmt, workspace clippy, aarch64 cross-clippy,\n`pixelflow-ir --no-default-features`, and the test suites for ir /\nsearch / codegen / core / graphics / compiler / pipeline / core-term all\nclean; `xtask isa-matrix --clippy --build-only` all three tiers\nBUILT+LINT; `cargo test -p pixelflow-codegen` under `+avx512f,+avx512dq`\nand under `+avx2,+fma` on an AVX-512 host clean.\n\nOn `7146468e`: fmt, workspace clippy, aarch64 cross-clippy, and the core\n/ core-term / graphics suites re-run clean.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
