          "id": "10c7daf40ccc444fb87f22a42879f7f8b7aeca8a",
          "message": "refactor(pixelflow-codegen): the allocator is handed the loop nest (#1119)\n\n## Summary\n\nStage 2 of `docs/plans/2026-09-01-loop-aware-codegen.md`. **Emitted code\nis byte-identical**; what changes is who is entitled to decide.\n\nThe emitter called `allocate` once per region and then worked out for\nitself which values crossed a back edge and where to park them. That\nmade loop-carried liveness the *emitter's* concept — which is precisely\nwhy it could only ever be answered one way: a fixed memory slot,\nwhatever the register pressure. `RegisterAllocator::allocate_nest` takes\nthe whole `ScopedSchedule` and returns one allocation per region plus\nthe carried values in slot order, so \"defined in one region, read in a\nregion inside it\" becomes an ordinary fact about liveness instead of a\nspecial case the emitter hand-manages.\n\nThe policy is unchanged — every carried value still gets a slot — which\nis exactly why the bytes do not move. That is the point of this stage:\n**stage 3 becomes a policy change in one place**, rather than a rewrite\nand a policy change at once.\n\n## Changes\n\n- **`ScopedSchedule` / `ScopeRegion` move from `emit` into `regalloc`.**\nThey are the allocator's input language now. `body` stays a separate\nfield rather than the last element of `regions`: it is inside every back\nedge, it produces the result, and it parks nothing — a list that could\nhold it would let the two be confused.\n- **`allocate_nest`** returns `NestAllocation { regions:\nVec<RegionAllocation>, body: Allocation }`, with `carried()` giving the\nslot order. Slots are named by **index, not offset** — where slot `k`\nsits depends on the scaffold's own frame, which is the emitter's\nbusiness and stays there.\n- **`presize_frame` deleted.** It existed to allocate every region a\nsecond time purely to learn its frame size; the nest allocation already\nholds them.\n- **`emit_dag_body_hoisted` takes a finished `Allocation`** instead of\nallocating internally, so allocation happens once, in one place, for the\nwhole kernel. `emit_dag_body` survives as a `#[cfg(test)]` one-region\nconvenience, which is now its only caller.\n\n## Validation\n\n- **Byte-identical** across a seven-kernel corpus: both hoist tiers, a\nY-only tier, a fully-invariant root (loop degenerates to a store), a\ntranscendental expansion, and a 14-value hoist under body pressure.\nHashes matched exactly before and after.\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --\n-D warnings`; aarch64 cross-clippy for codegen + core; test suites for\ncodegen / core / graphics / search — all clean.\n- ISA matrix and the AVX-512 / AVX2 codegen runs are in flight and will\nbe reported before merge.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
