          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c06aa3f608fc4ee817c8d049aaa2db50ec99dac4",
          "message": "test(pixelflow-search): pin the representational gap between the additive and bilinear Guides, and register the claim (#1123)\n\n## The finding\n\nEvery Phase 3 Guide measurement this week ran `LinearCandidateGuide`.\nReading `LinearWeights::logit` term by term:\n\n```\ns(r, x) = bias + w_rule[r] + w_budget*b + w_match_class*ln(1+m)\n        + w_neighborhood*ln(1+n) + w_expr_size*ln(1+e) + Σ_op w_op[op]*ln(1+c_op)\n```\n\nExactly one term names the rule, and it names nothing else. The score is\n**additively separable**, `s(r, x) = w_rule[r] + g(x)`, so the\nrule-by-context second difference is identically zero:\n\n```\n[s(r1,x) − s(r2,x)] − [s(r1,x') − s(r2,x')] = 0    for all r1, r2, x, x'\n```\n\nNo context can reorder two rules against each other. That is exactly the\nshape of the program's central question — \"the pythagorean identities\nare useless for bezier curves, but i sure as shit want them firing for\nspherical harmonics\" — so **the model class every measurement ran cannot\nrepresent the hypothesis round 1b tested.**\n\nThe budget term cannot rescue it. `egraph::guided` reads the application\nordinal once per round, before walking that round's matches, so every\ncandidate in one `score_candidates` batch shares a `budget_fraction`;\nthe consumer sorts descending with no threshold. A per-batch constant\nmoves the absolute score and moves no decision.\n\nThe bilinear tower already on `main` (`SaturationHead::score_candidate`\n→ `bilinear_score` = `m(x)ᵀWr + bᵀr`) is linear in the rule embedding\nwith **context-dependent coefficients**, so its rule-pair difference\ndepends on the context. Nothing implements `SaturationGuide` with it.\n\n## What this changes about the prior results — stated without\noverclaiming\n\nRound 1b's H_null and round 1's linear-ties-control are **consistent\nwith** an unrepresentable hypothesis. That is weaker than \"caused by\".\nThe data cannot distinguish:\n\n- *context does not matter* — a global rule prior is the right model;\nfrom\n- *this model cannot use context* — rule value is context-dependent and\nthe measured class has zero capacity for it.\n\nUnder the second, the additive model produces the H_null signature for a\nreason having nothing to do with the corpus. §2 of the registration says\nexactly this and no more.\n\nTwo nearby facts recorded, not claimed: round 1's *pure rule lookup*\ncontrol beating the candidate-feature arm is the predicted consequence\nof the functional form (the additive arm's rule ordering **is** a rule\nlookup); and the `dag_cost` oracle re-run finds rule-granularity\nhindsight-perfect filtering **indistinguishable from unguided** through\nB=400, while headroom is larger than round 1 believed (29.18% median\nregret still at B=800).\n\n## What is in this PR\n\n**`pixelflow-search/src/nnue/guide/scoring/representation.rs`** — five\ntests, over the *same* two candidate sets through the *same*\n`SaturationGuide::score_candidates` seam, so model class is the only\nthing varying:\n\n| test | pins |\n|---|---|\n| `additive_guide_should_induce_the_same_rule_order_in_every_context` |\nidentical rule order in a trig- and a polynomial-shaped neighborhood,\nwith a non-vacuity assertion that the contexts reach the model |\n|\n`additive_guide_should_have_an_identically_zero_rule_by_context_interaction`\n| second difference is zero, and equals `w_rule[r1] − w_rule[r2]` |\n|\n`additive_guide_budget_term_should_shift_every_score_equally_and_reorder_nothing`\n| budget shifts every score by `w_budget·Δ`, reorders nothing |\n| `bilinear_head_should_reorder_two_rules_between_two_contexts` | a\nhand-set head **swaps** the same two rules between the same two contexts\n|\n| `both_model_classes_score_the_same_candidate_sets_through_one_trait` |\nboth arms are `SaturationGuide`s over identical inputs |\n\nHand-set weights, not trained: a statement about the functional form,\nnot a training claim.\n\n**`docs/plans/2026-09-02-bilinear-guide-registration.md`** — committed\n*before* any bilinear Guide exists.\n\n- **Statistic (pre-committed):** round 1b's `D_A(S,B) = m_A^S(B) −\nm_A^DEV(B)`, all costs `ExtractedDAG::dag_cost`.\n- **Claim (H_repr):** `D_linear(sh,B) − D_bilinear(sh,B) > M_B` **and**\n`|D_linear(bezier,B) − D_bilinear(bezier,B)| ≤ M_B` — the second\nconjunct is what makes it *domain-conditional* rather than a capacity\nwin, and `H_capacity` is named now so it cannot be invented later. Plus\na DEV-not-wrecked conjunct and `n ≥ 30`.\n- **Margins:** M_100 = 0.06 / M_200 = 0.07, inherited **frozen** from\nthe round-1b registration.\n- **Instrument:** every reference median is re-measured on `dag_cost`\n(the tree-cost constants are not reproducible under #1117/#1118). The\ntree-cost-calibrated margin is carried with a pre-commitment that can\nonly make acceptance *harder*: recompute the DEV family swing on\n`dag_cost`, and if it exceeds `M_B`, declare the tier underpowered —\nnever raise the margin.\n- **Arms:** unguided (reference), `PerRuleRateGuide` (frozen),\n`LinearCandidateGuide` @ `guide_checkpoint_strict_v1.json` (frozen),\n`BilinearCandidateGuide` (new).\n- **Sets/tiers:** DEV classical, `sh` (primary), `bezier`; B=100/200\ninherited.\n- **§8 pre-writes the honest null:** a tie means the functional form is\nnot the bottleneck — look to the features (a 1-hop op multiset is\ntopology-blind) or to the label (a rule-marginal target admits no\ncontext-conditional form). It explicitly does *not* license \"context\ndoes not matter\".\n\nThe registrations it cites are frozen and unedited. FINAL untouched.\nFrozen strict-v1 and R2G checkpoints unchanged.\n\n## No production behavior change\n\nProduction leaves `guide: None`. §10 gates on the 206-kernel\n`production_extraction_digest` TSVs being byte-identical across any\nchange made under this registration.\n\n## Gates\n\nbuild ✅ · `test --workspace` ✅ (40/40 binaries green) · `clippy\n--workspace --all-targets -D warnings` ✅ · `fmt --check` ✅ · `check -p\npixelflow-ir --no-default-features` ✅ · `check -p pixelflow-search\n--no-default-features` ✅ · `check-provenance-journal-scope.sh` ✅\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-authored-by: JP Pittman <jppittman@jpptech.dev>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
