          "distinct": true,
          "id": "89fabf650df982a20e77b8a86d637165f33f5a27",
          "message": "perf(pixelflow-codegen): ymm10 was reserved by inheritance, not by use (#1131)\n\n## Summary\n\nEscape-hatches step 1 left exactly one register unaccounted for, and\nstep 1's whole point was that the accounting is now checkable. Every\nother ymm is named by `inputs`, `scratch`, `reload`, `select_reload` or\n`fixed`. **ymm10 was named by none of them.**\n\nIt is `x86_64::X86_SCRATCH` — the SSE2 backend's two-operand hazard temp\nand select blend temp — and AVX2 reaches neither:\n\n- VEX is non-destructive, so there is no two-operand hazard\n(`emit_binary_safe` is the SSE2 path only).\n- Its select is a VEX blend with no internal temp — `avx2::emit_select`,\nnot the shared one.\n- The one shared helper it does call, `x86_64::emit_gather_scalar`,\nnever touches `X86_SCRATCH`.\n\nTraced to a *read* rather than trusted to a name, which is the\ndiscipline the plan asks for and the same method that found two of the\nthree \"collisions\" in step 1 were phantom.\n\n## Effect\n\n| backend | pool before | pool after |\n|---|---|---|\n| SSE2 | 6 / 16 | 6 / 16 |\n| **AVX2** | **4 / 16** | **5 / 16** |\n| AVX-512 | 22 / 32 | 22 / 32 |\n| aarch64 | 15 / 32 | 15 / 32 |\n\n25% more registers for the backend that needed it most: AVX2 pays two\nregisters to ymm8/ymm9 for its gather's half-temporaries, which is why\nit sat below SSE2's six despite being the same physical file. After\nthis, all four pools are exhausted — every further register has to come\nfrom escape-hatches step 2 (temps and reloads becoming allocated\nvalues).\n\n## Validation\n\nCodegen suite run under `-C target-feature=+avx2,+fma` — the only build\nwhere this backend's code actually executes — all green. Plus `cargo fmt\n--all --check`, workspace clippy, the aarch64 cross-clippy, and the\ndefault-tier codegen/core suites.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
