          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1010737e20e8dbecdf053c1df17f8de7333fa9bb",
          "message": "feat(pixelflow-codegen): an instruction temp is an allocated value, not a reserved register (#1137)\n\n## Summary\n\nEscape-hatches step 2, the temps half (class A).\n\nA backend that needs a scratch register to express one instruction — a\nsign mask for `Neg`/`Abs`, a Newton-Raphson correction for\n`Rsqrt`/`Recip` — used to take a register for the **whole kernel**,\nbecause one instruction in it might want one.\n`RegisterFile::temps_for(&ScheduledOp) -> u8` declares the demand per op\ninstead; the allocator reserves a slot for exactly one instruction, and\n`InstructionPlan::temp` hands it to the encoder. `UNARY_SCRATCH` is gone\nfrom AVX2, AVX-512 and aarch64.\n\nThe temp is reserved **before** the destination is placed and excludes\nevery operand — the encoder writes it while the operands are still live\nand before it writes `dst`, so it can share a register with neither.\n\n## Pool effect\n\nStated as measured rather than as hoped:\n\n| backend | before | after | why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SSE2 | 6 | 6 | still `no_temps` — see below |\n| AVX2 | 5 | 5 | its `UNARY_SCRATCH` **was** `GATHER_IDX` |\n| AVX-512 | 22 | **23** | zmm15 joins the pool |\n| aarch64 | 15 | **16** | v29 joins the pool |\n\nAVX2 gains no register because ymm15 wore two names: it appeared in\n`fixed` twice, once as the gather's index and once as the unary mask.\nThe sign mask and the select blend had been *borrowing the gather's\nregister* — safe only because no single instruction is both, which is\nexactly the kind of convention step 1 exists to make checkable. What\nlands there is one owner per register, not a larger pool.\n\nSSE2 keeps `X86_SCRATCH` deliberately. Its two-operand hazard\n(`emit_binary_safe`) and decomposed `MulAdd` demand a scratch as a\nfunction of *which registers allocation picked* (`dst == right`), not of\nthe op — so the demand cannot be stated as `temps_for` yet, and drawing\na second pool register for the unary mask meanwhile would cost pressure\nand free nothing.\n\n## A temp cannot spill\n\nEvery *value* survives a small pool by going to memory, which is why a\none-register budget used to be legal. Scratch the encoder destroys\nmid-instruction has no such escape, so the pool must hold a ternary's\nthree operands plus the temp. That floor is `RegisterFile::MIN_SCRATCH =\n4`, asserted in `checked()` and clamped in `capped()` —\n`EmitCtx::max_regs` can no longer reach through it.\n\nFound by probe, not by reasoning: `with_max_regs(1)` on a `Neg` of a\ncomputed value hit the `unreachable!` arm on AVX2 and AVX-512. Worth\nstating plainly, since the first draft of the doc comment asserted the\ncase could not arise.\n\n## One test's premise, not its claim\n\nThe floor invalidated `a_spilled_muladd_rounds_twice_on_every_target`.\nIt reached the decomposed arm only because a one-register pool spills\nwhatever it is holding — the allocator evicts by Belady, and with the\n`MulAdd` in the middle the wall *outlived* the multiplicands, so the\nwall is what spilled. Moving the `MulAdd` last makes the multiplicands\nthe furthest-out values; the pressure now comes from the live ranges\nrather than from the pool being a single register, and the test forces\ndecomposition at any pool size.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test --workspace` — 132 suites green\n- codegen suite additionally under `-C target-feature=+avx2,+fma` and\n`+avx512f,+avx512dq`\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, workspace clippy, aarch64 cross-clippy\n\nNew unit tests cover the temp colliding with neither operand nor\ndestination, an op that asks for none getting none, the temp returning\nto the pool at the next instruction, and `capped` holding the floor.\n\n## Not in this change\n\nReload defs (class C) — `Placement::Spilled` and\n`reload`/`select_reload` are still there. That is where step 2's \"pool\nroughly doubles\" prediction actually lives.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-02T22:30:07-07:00",
