          "message": "feat(pixelflow-codegen): the gathers' scratch was reserved per kernel for an instruction most kernels lack (#1140)\n\n## Summary\n\nEscape-hatches step 2, and with it **class A is closed**. `Scratch`\ncarries up to `MAX_TEMPS` registers instead of one, so an encoding can\nask for several, and every gather's scratch became a per-instruction\nreservation.\n\nThe gathers were the last of class A. A 256-bit AVX2 gather needs four\nregisters — a 128-bit half's index and value, plus one of each to carry\nthe high half while the low one is assembled — AVX-512 and SSE2 two,\naarch64 one. Each was held out of the pool for the *whole kernel*, for\nan instruction most kernels do not contain at all.\n\n## Pool\n\n| backend | pool at step 1 | now | of |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| SSE2 | 6 | **9** | 16 |\n| AVX2 | 4 | **10** | 16 |\n| AVX-512 | 6 | **26** | 32 |\n| aarch64 | 10 | **17** | 32 |\n\nEvery one is past the \"pool could be\" column in the plan's accounting\ntable (8 / 8 / 22 / 15) — that column was drawn before temps were\nallocatable, so it still charged each backend for the registers its own\nencodings borrow.\n\n`fixed` is now **empty** on AVX2 and AVX-512, and holds exactly one\nregister on SSE2 (`X86_SCRATCH`, whose demand is a function of *which\nregisters allocation picked* rather than of the op) and one on aarch64\n(`GUARD_SCRATCH`).\n\n`MIN_SCRATCH` rose from 4 to 6, and its reason moved with it: no longer\na ternary's three operands plus a temp, but AVX2's gather — one operand\nplus four temps — with room for the destination either way.\n\n## Four tests that had stopped testing anything\n\nThree had a pool size written in as a literal:\n\n- `muladd_and_clamp_spilled` said *\"Sethi-Ullman number > 6\"*, which\nstopped exceeding the pool the moment the pool grew. It now sizes its\nfillers from `pool_size()`.\n- `belady_evicts_the_value_used_farthest_out` and\n`the_pool_may_straddle_a_reserved_register` are now stated in terms of\n`MIN_SCRATCH`.\n\nThe fourth was worse than stale.\n`a_spilled_muladd_rounds_twice_on_every_target` built its wall from `(l\n− r) − (l − r)` — which `legalize` folds to a single constant, so\n**there was no wall**. It reached the decomposed arm only because the\npool was smaller than the three values it did keep live. Its terms are\nnow `(X + i) · W`: worth exactly zero at W = 0, and not foldable,\nbecause a variable is the one thing the folder cannot see through.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `cargo test --workspace` — 132 suites green\n- codegen suite additionally under `-C target-feature=+avx2,+fma` and\n`+avx512f,+avx512dq`\n- `cargo fmt --all --check`, workspace clippy, aarch64 cross-clippy\n\nThe gather paths are the risk here, and they are covered end-to-end\nagainst the interpreter by `collapse_loop.rs`, which executes them on\nevery tier.\n\n## Not in this change\n\nThe rest of class C — `Placement::Spilled` and `reload`. Its blocker is\nrecorded in the plan: eviction marks a value spilled for its *whole\nlife*, so residency read when reserving is not final, and closing it\nmeans a fixed point over forced spills (or live-range splitting) rather\nthan another field.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
