          "distinct": true,
          "id": "eef1482c5a2337f301b4d0e2c3bb40d897bc9db2",
          "message": "docs(plans): record the ranged-placement landing, and why it precedes the policy (#1149)\n\nDocs only. Adds the landing block for #1148 to\n`docs/plans/2026-09-01-register-allocation-escape-hatches.md`, in the\nsame form as the five 2026-09-03 blocks before it:\n\n- what landed: `Placement` as a sequence of spans over nest-wide\n`Point`s, one placement map per nest, `carries` deleted, byte-identical\non 61 kernels × 3 pools × 3 tiers;\n- where the spec was wrong about the code, both pinned by tests (leaves\nare scheduled in both scopes; a carried root needs two spans);\n- what stayed per scope (`FrameLayout`) and why;\n- why this is the step *before* the policy: the two measured negatives\n(frequency weighting +37%, whole-life splitting's guarded-region hole)\nask for the same design — one pool over the nest, splitting on eviction,\nstore at the definition, reloads that keep their register, head\nreconciliation — and that design needs exactly this output shape. Same\ntrait, same types. Not graph coloring, and it says why.\n\nNo code changes. The policy work itself is being implemented against a\nwritten spec and will arrive as a separate PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
