          "distinct": true,
          "id": "cd6000ebf9df79617b37751b7dc58580c9acf28e",
          "message": "docs(plans): one pool over the nest, as a flat pass, measured worse — and what the budget was actually doing (#1152)\n\nDocs only: a measured negative result, recorded in\n`docs/plans/2026-09-01-register-allocation-escape-hatches.md` next to\nthe two before it.\n\nThe third piece of the splitting design — regions and body allocated in\none forward pass over nest-wide program points, roots live to the tail,\nthe carry budget deleted — was built in full after #1150, passes every\nsuite at SSE2, and is **+14% bytes / +26% memory ops** on the 259-kernel\nglyph corpus with Belady over the flat index, and **+40% / +276%** with\nloop-carried lives made un-evictable. Not merged; kept as a `wip` commit\non the implementing agent's branch so the implementation and the\nmeasurement survive.\n\nThe block records:\n\n- where the denotation was wrong: Belady's distance in the flat index\ncounts *static* positions and an eviction costs *dynamic* ones, so a\nflat pass evicts the root first;\n- that both directions of pricing have now been measured (depth\nweighting over-carries, flat distance under-carries, pinning\nover-carries worse), and that the carry budget was doing more than\nbraking;\n- the four pieces of that commit that are right regardless\n(per-definition lives, placeholders as neither definitions nor\nconstants, scratch exclusion by location rather than ownership, the\nemitter following a moving live-in);\n- the next step, which is neither a weight nor a tier: replace the `pool\n− MIN_SCRATCH` constant with the body's *measured* peak demand, and\npre-color carried roots into the region scan so the choice stops\ndepending on what the region happens to leave free.\n\nNo code changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
