          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1673e847df069cd0b768a79d4b5760e08421dc53",
          "message": "docs(plans): two more carry-budget replacements measured; the constant stands (#1153)\n\nDocs only: the closing measurement block for the carry-budget line in\n`docs/plans/2026-09-01-register-allocation-escape-hatches.md`.\n\nAfter the flat one-pool pass (#1152), two further designs to remove the\n`pool − MIN_SCRATCH` carry budget were built in full by a delegated\nagent and verified by a second, independent one:\n\n- **3′** — budget from the body's measured peak demand, carried roots\npre-colored into the region scan, parked roots pinned to slots instead\nof a placeholder holding a body register.\n- **3″** — the same, with carries accepted only when measured *dynamic\nmemory ops per call* fall, using trip counts plumbed from the\n`LatticeShape` that `jit_cache::compile` already keys on but never\nhanded to the emitter.\n\nBoth lower static memory ops on the glyph corpus (SSE2 −9.2% dynamic ops\nfor 3″). Both raise AVX-512 code size ~19%, and 3″ measures **+13–18%\nwall clock** on the glyph bench there, outside the run-to-run spread.\nVerification found that the trip-count pricing never refused a single\ncandidate on either tier — the budget clipped everything first — and\nthat static memory ops do not predict time on the wide tier.\n\nConclusion recorded: the existing budget (#1147/#1150) is the\nbest-measured policy on every tier by wall clock and stays; the\ntrip-count plumbing is the right denotation and is preserved on a branch\nrather than landed unused; and what would change the conclusion is a\ncost model whose prediction tracks wall clock across tiers, measured\nbefore any policy is built on it.\n\nBranches preserved (unpushed, in the session's worktree):\n`one-pool-flat-814710c2`, `measured-budget-be33ec66`, and 355f1ff1 on\n`worktree-agent-a4cec4140409ecfc2`.\n\nNo code changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
