          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e6bc17b3b77048fe41bd278f3ce48dea55dbe15a",
          "message": "docs(plans): a kernel with a lattice is the only evaluation API (#1164)\n\nDocs only: the plan of record for the direction stated today —\n**per-batch evaluation is not an API.** The only way a consumer turns a\nkernel into numbers is `Lattice::bake(&Kernel)` for a field or its\npacked-pixel form for a frame, one collapse call per stripe, stripes\nacross threads.\n\nThe plan records:\n\n- **The measurement.** On the same shader and lattice, the JIT is 1.1×\n(SSE2) to **1.98× (AVX-512) slower** than the `kernel!` expression\ntemplates through the per-batch `eval` boundary, and **1.4× to 2.35×\nfaster** through the collapse loop. The 2× is the ABI; the compiler\nalready wins without it because it hoists row-invariant work the\ntemplates recompute per batch. Production (cell grid, glyphs) is already\non the collapse path.\n- **The inventory**: every per-batch surface (`kernel_jit!`'s `Manifold`\nwrapper, `JitManifold::eval_*`, `Lattice::collapse*`, `Scene::Surface`\nand the rasterizer's `execute_stripe` family, the Rust-side\n`Discrete::pack`) and what replaces each.\n- **The one thing that cannot lower yet**: scene3d's ray marching needs\nan iteration binder the IR does not have. Two ways to close it (add\n`Iterate`, or retire the demos); until decided, `Scene::Surface` is the\nonly permitted per-batch remnant.\n- **Three stages**, each gated on the same shader measured before and\nafter.\n\nNo code changes. S1 and S2 are being implemented against this plan by\ndelegated agents.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV)_\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-05T18:47:51-07:00",
