          "distinct": true,
          "id": "c291db06a0ecf3ef33b349a5a84330d5654184f2",
          "message": "perf(codegen): a choice between colours is one select, and a guard clusters its arm — S3b (#1177)\n\nStage S3b of docs/plans/2026-09-06-kernel-with-a-lattice.md. The\nchrome-scene gate S3 missed is met on both tiers: packed 43.9 -> 12.2\nns/px single-threaded on SSE2 and 16.0 -> 4.8 on AVX-512, ahead of the\nlegacy tier at every thread count (1.13-1.75x). No golden moved.\n\nLanguage half: Bits::select in pixelflow-ir (Select is already a bitwise\nblend; same node, honest type), and a colour in pixelflow-graphics is a\ntree of four channel kernels at the leaves and choices at the nodes, so\nHit::select is one select whose arm holds the whole reflected world.\n\nCodegen half: cluster_select_arms partitions a select's region into\nshared, true-exclusive, false-exclusive so a refused arm becomes a\ncontiguous guarded range (sinking what the select does not read);\nexclusivity is a closure to a fixed point, fixing a latent miscompile\nthat contiguity had been hiding; and an arm is guarded only when its\nlatency-prior cost exceeds MISPREDICT_PENALTY_CYCLES, a bound that caps\nany guard's downside at its upside. A guard-coverage instrument\n(PIXELFLOW_GUARD_TELEMETRY) reports what fires.\n\nCorpus (208 kernels): clock sign improves on both tiers; the small glyph\nkernels that regressed up to 3.6x before the bound are within noise\nafter it. Recorded: dyn_memory_ops cannot see a skipped range, and mask\ncoherence is the first profile-dependent term for the schedule-cost\nresidual.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eji8JfyLCcTRmbbhyQCvWV",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-06T05:29:44-07:00",
          "tree_id": "9c6fce7c45255b17dd27c45e5405de015137c8cc",
          "url": "https://github.com/jppittman/pixelflow/commit/c291db06a0ecf3ef33b349a5a84330d5654184f2"
