          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e2474c7e09da7aed2dd5dd5861d61cca1de0b4b4",
          "message": "fix(ci): pixelflow-compiler is not a bench target (#1497)\n\n## What\n\n`Benchmark Regression Check` still fails on main after #1495. That fix\nremoved `desloppify` from the bench run, which let `cargo bench\n--workspace --benches -- --output-format bencher` reach the next crate\nwith the same problem: `pixelflow-compiler`'s proc-macro lib, whose\nlibtest harness rejects `--output-format`. Run 703 on `68276a5` failed\nthere (`error: bench failed, to rerun pass -p pixelflow-compiler\n--lib`).\n\n## Fix\n\n`bench = false` on `pixelflow-compiler`'s `[lib]`, the same as every\nother crate. This is a manifest fix, not an assertion problem: the crate\nhas no benches.\n\n## Verified\n\nReproduced and checked locally with the CI flag:\n\n- Without the change, `cargo bench -p pixelflow-compiler --benches --\n--output-format bencher` runs `unittests src/lib.rs` and fails with\n`Unrecognized option: 'output-format'` (exit 101).\n- With the change it reports \"no targets matched\" (exit 0).\n\n`pixelflow-compiler` was the only crate whose `[lib]` lacked `bench =\nfalse`. I checked every `Cargo.toml`: all other libs and the\n`core-term`, `desloppify` and `xtask` bins already have it.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WjvQDtBKfhuaePoevjyyt7)_\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
